From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 9991: make `ubus call map.agent status` parse

`ubus call map.agent status` is not valid JSON on any node that has a backhaul
STA MLD, which is every agent. Measured 2026-08-01 on all three nodes:

  4g (controller)  jsonfilter -e '@.ap_mld[*].ifname'  ->  ap-mld-2 ap-mld-1
  8g (agent)       jsonfilter                          ->  Failed to parse JSON
  x8 (agent)       jsonfilter                          ->  Failed to parse JSON

The controller only escapes because it runs no bSTA MLD, so its "bsta_mld"
comes out as an empty table and happens to be well formed.

"bsta_mld" is opened as a table and then holds an unkeyed table, which libubox
renders as

	"bsta_mld": {
		{
			"ifname": "bsta-mld-3",

There is exactly one backhaul STA MLD per node - agent->bstamld is a single
pointer - so the object is right and the anonymous wrapper inside it is not.
Dropping the wrapper keeps the empty case unchanged ("bsta_mld": {}) and makes
the populated case parse. The closing call is corrected to close_table for the
same reason.

This is the second site of the defect 982 fixed in the backhaul block; the
handoff of 2026-07-31 listed it as open item 5.

The same function has a third instance waiting to happen, fixed here too: in
the mld_stations loop the table is opened before agent_get_sta(), and the !s
path continues without closing it. It needs a client to disappear between the
affiliated list being built and the status being rendered, which is why it has
not been seen yet - it would produce exactly the same unparseable output, but
only sometimes.

Consumers that had to work around this can stop. mld-report-check counts
affiliated APs with awk for this reason and says so in a comment; the workaround
stays until this patch has been on the nodes long enough to trust.

--- a/src/agent.c	2026-08-01 12:19:30.315059325 +0200
+++ b/src/agent.c	2026-08-01 12:19:30.315106741 +0200
@@ -6180,11 +6180,18 @@
 				void *ttttt;
 				struct sta *s;
 
-				ttttt = blobmsg_open_table(&bb, "");
+				/* Look up first, open second. The other way round,
+				 * a station that has gone away since the MLD's
+				 * affiliated list was built leaves a table open
+				 * that nothing ever closes - the same unparseable
+				 * output as above, arriving only when a client
+				 * roams at the wrong moment.
+				 */
 				s = agent_get_sta(agent, smld->affiliated_sta[i]);
 				if (!s)
 					continue;
 
+				ttttt = blobmsg_open_table(&bb, "");
 				blobmsg_add_macaddr(&bb, "macaddr", s->macaddr);
 				blobmsg_add_macaddr(&bb, "bssid", s->bssid);
 				blobmsg_add_u32(&bb, "linkid", s->mlo_link_id);
@@ -6204,8 +6211,24 @@
 		void *aa;
 		int i;
 
-		t = blobmsg_open_table(&bb, "");
-
+		/* No anonymous table here. A node has one backhaul STA MLD -
+		 * agent->bstamld is a single pointer - so this is an object,
+		 * and an unkeyed object nested inside it is what libubox
+		 * renders as
+		 *
+		 *	"bsta_mld": {
+		 *		{
+		 *			"ifname": "bsta-mld-3",
+		 *
+		 * which is not JSON. jsonfilter rejects the whole document
+		 * with "quoted object property name expected", so every
+		 * consumer of map.agent status loses every field, not just
+		 * this one. Measured 2026-08-01: both agents unparseable,
+		 * the controller parseable only because it has no bsta_mld
+		 * and the empty table is well formed by accident.
+		 *
+		 * Same defect as 982 in the backhaul block, second site.
+		 */
 		blobmsg_add_string(&bb, "ifname", agent->bstamld->bk.ifname);
 		blobmsg_add_macaddr(&bb, "macaddr", agent->bstamld->bk.macaddr);
 		blobmsg_add_macaddr(&bb, "bssid", agent->bstamld->bk.bssid);
@@ -6236,10 +6259,8 @@
 			blobmsg_close_table(&bb, tt);
 		}
 		blobmsg_close_array(&bb, aa);
-
-		blobmsg_close_table(&bb, t);
 	}
-	blobmsg_close_array(&bb, a);
+	blobmsg_close_table(&bb, a);
 #endif
 	ubus_send_reply(ctx, req, bb.head);
 	blob_buf_free(&bb);
